{
  "text": "2015A05 Sevoflurane and fentanyl are a common anaesthetic drug\ncombination.\nDiscuss pharmacological reasons why it is useful to use them together.\nList:\n·\nSummary\n·\nDrug effects\n·\nPD\n·\nPK\n·\nPC\nSummary:\nPharmacodynamic (PD)\nComplementary and synergistic -> ↓dose -> ↓side effects\nPharmacokinetic (PK)\nSynergy -> ↓dose -> ↓accumulation\nNo interference\nPharmaceutics (PC)\nNo incompatibility\nDrug effects:\nSevoflurane (SF)\nFentanyl (F)\nAmnesia\nMAC 0.25\nUnreliable even at high Ce\nHypnosis\nMAC 0.3\nImmobility\nMAC 1\nNo\nAnalgesia\nNo\nYes\nCVS side effects\n↓HR, ↓contractility, ↓SVR, ↓mAP\n↓SNS output -> ↓HR, ↓SVR, ↓mAP\nResp side effects\n↑RR, ↓TV\n↓RR, ↓TV\nOther\nPONV\n↑Uterine blood flow +/- PPH\n↑Cerebral blood flow +/- ICP\nPONV\nSedation\nPharmacodynamics:\nComplementary\n·\nSF: anaesthesia\n·\nF: analgesia\nSynergistic\n·\nCombined effect exceeds sum of individual\n  effects\n·\nRepresented by isobologram (or response\n  surface)\n·\nMechanism: ? F reduces nociceptive activation\n  of ascending reticular activating system (ARAS)\nImplications of synergism\n·\n↓SF % for hypnosis and immobility\n·\n↓MAC standard deviation -> ↓variability\n·\n↓SF side effects\n·\n↓Need for paralysis\nQuantification of interaction\nSF alone\nSF + F 3ng/mL\nMACBAR\n4.15%\n↓80%\nMAC\n1.85%\n↓60%\nMACawake\n0.6%\n↓25%\nStandard deviation\n0.1MAC\n<0.1MAC (not from this stud\nhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9447851\nhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/?term=fentanyl+sevoflurane+somatic+1999\nPharmacokinetics:\nLack of interference\n·\nPlasma protein binding sites:\no\nFentanyl to AAG > albumin\no\nSevoflurane uptake to proteins, lipids, RBCs\n·\nMetabolism:\no\nSF -> liver CYP2E1 (only 2-5%)\no\nF -> liver CYP3A4 (almost 100%)\n·\nExcretion:\no\nSF via lungs\no\nF metabolites via urine\nImplications of synergism\n·\nFor a given desired effect, ↓[SF] and ↓[F]\n·\n↓compartmental concentrations\n·\n↓total dose, ↓accumulation\n·\n↓time to emergence (since MAC awake less\n  affected)\nPharmaceutics:\nCompatibility\nNone: F intravenous, SF inhaled\nEfficiency\nSynergism -> ↓total dose -> ↓cost\nFeedback welcome\nat\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
